    "text": "The surface of certain metal is first illuminated with light of wavelength <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>350</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>n</mn><mn>m</mn></math> and then, by a light of wavelength <math><msub><mrow><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>540</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>n</mn><mn>m</mn><mo>.</mo></math> It is found that the maximum speed of the photoelectrons in the two cases differ by a factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.&nbsp;The work function of the metal (in <math><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></math>) is close to<br />\r(Energy of photon <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1240</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>e</mn><mn>V</mn></math> )"
